# Comments

Do not add a comment that restates the code. A comment earns its place only by recording something a reader cannot recover from the code and would otherwise undo: a constraint, a rejected alternative, a non-obvious requirement of an external API. Write the why, never the what. Applies to source, YAML and workflows, shell, and config alike.

- **Default to no comment.** If a line needs explaining, rename or restructure first; a comment is the fallback.
- **Never write a comment for an AI reader.** Path-scoped rules (`.claude/rules/`, mirrored in `.cursor/rules/`) are that channel: they cost context only when a matching file is touched, while a comment costs context on every read, forever.
- An explanation longer than two lines, or one that applies to more than the line below it, belongs in a rule, not a comment block at the top of a file.
- **Keep the comments that prevent a regression:** why a key is deliberately absent, why a non-default value is set, why an apparently redundant line is load-bearing. Test: deleting it should feel risky; if deleting it changes nothing, it should not be there.

## Do not generate

These fail the test above. Never add them; when you touch a file that has them, delete them - but do not hunt them in files you are not editing, and do not rewrite working code just to make a comment deletable.

- Restating the next statement, control flow, or a well-named symbol (`// increment i`, `/** Resolve the allowlist. */` on `resolveCorsOrigins`).
- Section banners, IDE/scaffold boilerplate, commented-out code (restore it or delete it).
- TODOs that are no longer actionable.
- File-header essays repeating a path-scoped rule or `AGENTS.md`.
- Config keys that restate the tool's default.
- Ignore, allow, or dictionary entries for tools or words the repo does not use.
- The same rationale repeated in every environment block - state it once, in a rule.
- Rationale in a turbo task `description`: one clause saying what the task does; the why lives in [../core/turborepo.mdc](../core/turborepo.mdc).

## Keep without re-litigating

- License headers and legally required notices.
- Generated-file banners (`.cloudflare/types/index.d.ts`, `routeTree.gen.ts`); never hand-edit those files ([guardrails.mdc](../core/guardrails.mdc)).
- Machine-read markers: `@internal` (tag only, no prose restating "for tests" - [knip.mdc](knip.mdc)), `oxlint-disable-*` with a reason ([code-style.mdc](code-style.mdc)), `// @vitest-environment …`, `@ts-expect-error` with a reason, workflow `# vX.Y.Z` SHA pins.
- JSDoc that is a public API contract or carries types tooling needs. Prose JSDoc that only repeats the name or signature is still a comment: delete it.

`knip.jsonc` stays comment-free; every override's rationale lives in [knip.mdc](knip.mdc).
